-- title:
--   Two full ℤ-lattices have equal local boxes almost everywhere
-- statement:
--   Let $D$ be a ring equipped with a $\mathbb Q$-algebra structure, and let $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ be $\mathbb Z$-submodules of $D$, each assumed finitely generated and each assumed to span $D$ over $\mathbb Q$, i.e. $\operatorname{span}_{\mathbb Q}(\Lambda_i)=\top$ for $i=1,2$. Here, for a $\mathbb Z$-submodule $\Lambda\subseteq D$ and a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ (a finite place of $\mathbb Q$), [`Submodule.localBox`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) $\Lambda\,v$ denotes the additive subgroup of $D\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ generated by the set of elements of the form $z\otimes c$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of the $v$-adic completion of $\mathbb Q$; the completion and its integers are taken in the `HeightOneSpectrum` formalism for the Dedekind domain $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a finite set $S$ of finite places of $\mathbb Q$ such that for every place $v\notin S$ the two additive subgroups coincide: [`Submodule.localBox`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) $\Lambda_1\,v=$ [`Submodule.localBox`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) $\Lambda_2\,v$ inside $D\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$.
--
--   This is the standard fact that two full $\mathbb Z$-lattices in a finite-dimensional $\mathbb Q$-algebra have the same local completions at all but finitely many finite places. It is used in the comparison of orders in quaternion algebras, where it allows local conjugators between maximal or Eichler orders to be taken trivial outside a finite set of places.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Submodule_exists_finset_forall_not_mem_localBox_eq.lean

